- If the operator registry has explicit upgrade targets, untargeted discovered primary axes default to locked.
- If this is an explicit plan command, or autonomous mode is on, and the registry has no explicit upgrade targets, upgrade primary axes that have a real current→target gap this repository can take now. Official latest is the research ceiling, not the automatic axis target. Lock primaries when the operator locked them, or an opened official page shows they are already the current safe/stable/LTS target, or a verified incompatibility in this repository blocks the next official step.
- Official upgrade/migration guides decide candidate checkpoints. Do not skip a step those pages list unless this repository cannot take it. A latest-only registry tag is not a guide: still open the upgrade-path page for that stack. If the guide lists stable intermediates between current and latest, keep one milestone per step that this repo can install and gate now, and chain depends_on. Drop a step that repo-invoked consumers or locked axes cannot consume. If no step remains, do not emit a milestone to the unreachable official latest. Do not invent versions. Do not reuse a ladder from another stack. One milestone per primary axis edge. Compatibility requirements are constraint edges, not permission to move another axis.
- A milestone means this step is expected to land in this repository. If repo-invoked consumers cannot take the proposed target, do NOT emit that milestone. Set the axis target to the last version this repo can actually take. Record CONSTRAINTS `blocked_at` for the unreachable official version with opened evidence. Put that newer official version in SOURCES as `opened:` plus why it cannot land here. Do not invent dual-install, aliases, or extra packages to force the step. If the operator explicitly targeted that unreachable version, emit the step and the constraint; writer may still BLOCK.
- Do not lock a primary axis merely because the operator did not type --target.
- Empty MILESTONES and GATES (header only) are allowed only when there are zero upgrade axes.
- Every milestone changes exactly one primary axis.
- Compatibility requirements are constraint edges, not permission to move another axis.
- Use one milestone row per safe version edge/checkpoint.
- Use `-` in depends_on when a milestone has no dependencies; do not leave that field empty.
- A bare manifest name (package.json, tsconfig.json, package-lock.json) in source_of_truth also covers that file in every subdirectory (monorepo workspaces); do not list each nested copy.
- Every axis MUST specify tracked repository-relative source_of_truth paths; separate multiple paths with |.
- source_of_truth is the allow-list of git paths this axis may change. If a manifest has a companion lockfile in the repository, list BOTH. Examples: composer.json|composer.lock ; package.json|package-lock.json ; Gemfile|Gemfile.lock ; go.mod|go.sum ; Cargo.toml|Cargo.lock ; pyproject.toml|poetry.lock ; mix.exs|mix.lock. Listing only the manifest fails the milestone when the lockfile is regenerated. CI files that pin the same axis also belong on that list.
- Every milestone MUST define all four gates; fast/milestone are mandatory and review_required=true.
- Gate commands are untrusted proposed shell code; only operator approve-plan freezes them. Never use a fake PASS command.
- Locked target must be the current version, never the word null.
- You must invoke fetch/search/browser tools for every discovered primary axis before writing AXES: the official current-release page, the official upgrade/migration guide, and official support/peer/compat pages for tools this repo actually invokes for that axis. Memory is not a substitute. A `/latest` registry body alone is not enough.
- If a tool is actually denied or times out AFTER you invoked it: do NOT lock the axis as already-current. If you can still name a strictly newer official version AND you have not shown that this repository cannot take it, set policy=upgrade to that version and emit a milestone. If repo-invoked consumers reject that version, do not emit the step. If you cannot name a newer version, omit a fake upgrade row and fail planning as unresolved research. Silent lock is forbidden. Same-version policy=upgrade is forbidden.
- policy=upgrade requires current != target and a milestone whose to= equals that target. Never write same-version policy=upgrade.
- Never write `model_knowledge` as the only evidence for an already-current lock. That lock requires a SOURCES row whose `what` starts with `opened:` and names the latest version the opened page showed.
- `opened fetch denied` is not live proof. Only `opened: <version>` counts.
- Do not invent nonexistent versions. Cargo is still not catalogued.
- Every primary axis except an explicit operator lock MUST have a SOURCES https URL. That includes axes you want to lock as already-current. `what` must start with `opened:`.
- For remote CI use pass_condition=sha-success: command must exit 0 and print exactly CI_SHA=<exact head SHA> and CI_STATUS=success on separate lines.
- If .github/workflows/*.yml exist in this repository, inspect them. If a repo-local CI poller script is already present (for example spike/ci-wait.sh or any committed script whose contract is "exit 0, print CI_SHA=<head> and CI_STATUS=success"), set full_ci required=true, pass_condition=sha-success, and command=<path to that script> --workflow <workflow file name> for the workflow(s) that actually run on push/PR for this repository's default branch. Do not invent a poller script that is not present in the repository; if none exists, leave full_ci as required=false, command=-.
EOF2
}

cmd_plan() {
  local option provider=''
  while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
    option="$1"
    case "$option" in
      --provider) [ $# -gt 1 ] || fail 'missing --provider value'; provider="$2"; shift 2 ;;
      --import) break ;;
      *) break ;;
    esac
  done
  if [ -z "${AI_UPGRADER_NO_WIPE:-}" ]; then
    start_fresh_session "${provider:-auto}"
    info 'Replanning; operator targets and provider kept'
  else
    load_state
    if [ -n "$provider" ]; then
      select_provider "$provider"
      write_state
    fi
    [ "$PROVIDER" != auto ] || select_provider auto
  fi
  [ "$PROVIDER" != manual ] || [ "${1:-}" = --import ] || fail 'manual provider requires plan --import'
  ensure_tables
  local prompt candidate
  prompt="$(base_policy)

PLAN TASK: 90-second discovery. Identify primary axes from the listed files. For each axis open the official current-release page and that stack's official upgrade/migration guide (the page that lists version hops — not a latest-only tag). Build milestones from those hops. Emit TSV, stop. Do not invent versions. Do not use context-mode/MCP. Do not modify the repository.

$(operator_registry_packet)

$(plan_path_hints)

DISCOVERY/PLAN ONLY. Do not modify repository files.
Operator upgrade authorization: ${UPGRADE_GOAL:-$DEFAULT_UPGRADE_GOAL}
This explicit plan command authorizes discovery the same way upgrade does. It does not write the repository.
Autonomous mode: $AUTO_MODE. Execution is a later upgrade/run step; this step is plan-only.
It NEVER authorizes changing an explicit lock.
If a requested target conflicts with a locked axis, report BLOCKED.

$(plan_schema_instruction)"
  candidate="$(mktemp "$TRUST_DIR/.candidate.XXXXXXXX")"
  if [ "${1:-}" = --import ]; then
    [ $# -eq 2 ] && [ -f "$2" ] || fail 'usage: plan --import <file>'
    cp "$2" "$candidate"
  else
    [ $# -eq 0 ] || fail 'usage: plan [--provider claude|codex|cursor] [--import <file>]'
    mkdir -p "$WORK_DIR/logs"
    : > "$WORK_DIR/logs/plan.cursor.ndjson"
    set +e
    AI_UPGRADER_STOP_WHEN_TSV=1 \
      AI_UPGRADER_CURSOR_RAW="$WORK_DIR/logs/plan.cursor.ndjson" \
      AI_UPGRADER_MODEL_TIMEOUT="${AI_UPGRADER_PLAN_TIMEOUT:-600}" \
      STREAM_HUMAN="$PLAN" stream_model "$candidate" invoke_readonly "$prompt"
    rc=$?
    set -e
    if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then
      [ -s "$candidate" ] && cp "$candidate" "$WORK_DIR/logs/plan.failed.md"
      if [ "$rc" -eq 124 ]; then
        fail "plan exceeded ${AI_UPGRADER_PLAN_TIMEOUT:-600}s; inspect $WORK_DIR/logs/plan.cursor.ndjson"
      fi
      fail "planner failed; inspect $WORK_DIR/logs/plan.cursor.ndjson"
    fi
    [ -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=normal)" ] \
      || fail 'planner modified the repository; planning is read-only'
  fi
  mkdir -p "$ARCHIVE_DIR" "$WORK_DIR/logs"
  cp "$candidate" "$PLAN_RAW"
  cp "$candidate" "$ARCHIVE_DIR/plan.failed.md"
  cp "$candidate" "$WORK_DIR/logs/plan.failed.md"
  write_human_plan_from "$candidate"
  normalize_plan_tables "$candidate"
  rm -f "$candidate" "$ARCHIVE_DIR/plan.failed.md" "$WORK_DIR/logs/plan.failed.md"
  cleanup_temp_artifacts
  PHASE="PLANNED"
  MILESTONE_ID=''; MILESTONE_AXIS=''; BASE_SHA=''; REVIEW_SHA=''
  FAST_GATE=NOT_RUN; MILESTONE_GATE=NOT_RUN; FULL_CI=NOT_RUN; SMOKE_GATE=NOT_RUN; REVIEW_STATUS=NOT_RUN
  APPROVED_PLAN_HASH=''
  LAST_KNOWN_GOOD_SHA="$(git rev-parse HEAD)"
  NEXT_ACTION="approve validated plan and its gate commands"
  write_state
  info "Plan validated."
  if [ -f "$AXES" ]; then
    awk -F '\t' 'NR>1 && $5=="upgrade" {printf "  upgrade  %s  %s -> %s\n", $1, $3, $4}' "$AXES"
    awk -F '\t' 'NR>1 && $5=="locked" {n++} END{if(n) printf "  locked   %d axes\n", n}' "$AXES"
  fi
  info "Details: $PLAN_YML"
}

plan_hash() {
  local f
  {
    # Hash the executable adapter, not status wrappers in YAML.
    # plan.yml status draft→ready must not invalidate approval.
    for f in "$TARGETS" "$AXES" "$CONSTRAINTS" "$MILESTONES" "$GATES"; do
      [ -f "$f" ] || fail "missing plan input: $f"
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(basename "$f")" "$(hash_file "$f")"
    done
    if [ -f "$SOURCES" ]; then
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(basename "$SOURCES")" "$(hash_file "$SOURCES")"
    fi
  } | hash_stream
}
assert_approved() {
  [ -n "$APPROVED_PLAN_HASH" ] || fail 'plan not operator approved'
  [ "$(plan_hash)" = "$APPROVED_PLAN_HASH" ] || fail 'approved plan/targets/gates changed; replan and approve'
}
cmd_approve_plan() {
  load_state
  apply_human_axes_md
  [ "$PHASE" = PLANNED ] || fail 'approve-plan requires PLANNED phase'
  [ -z "$MILESTONE_ID" ] || fail 'cannot approve during a milestone'
  require_clean
  [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$LAST_KNOWN_GOOD_SHA" ] || fail 'HEAD changed since plan; replan'
  [ -f "$PLAN_YML" ] && [ -f "$MANIFEST_YML" ] && [ -f "$GATES_YML" ] || fail 'canonical YAML plan missing'
  persist_canonical_yaml
  sync_adapter_from_canonical
  APPROVED_PLAN_HASH="$(plan_hash)"
  NEXT_ACTION='start a milestone with begin/run; frozen gates are now executable'
  write_state
  info "Operator plan approval recorded: $APPROVED_PLAN_HASH"
}

require_clean() {
  [ -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=normal)" ] || fail 'working tree is dirty; commit or preserve unrelated changes before validation'
}

verify_base_anchor() {
  local ref anchored
  [ -n "${MILESTONE_ID:-}" ] && [ -n "${BASE_SHA:-}" ] || return 0
  valid_identifier "$MILESTONE_ID" || fail 'invalid active milestone id'
  ref="refs/ai-upgrader/$MILESTONE_ID/base"
  anchored="$(git rev-parse --verify "$ref" 2>/dev/null || true)"
  if [ -z "$anchored" ]; then
    git update-ref "$ref" "$BASE_SHA" "" || fail "cannot anchor immutable BASE_SHA for $MILESTONE_ID"
  elif [ "$anchored" != "$BASE_SHA" ]; then
    fail "immutable BASE_SHA mismatch for $MILESTONE_ID: state=$BASE_SHA anchor=$anchored"
  fi
}

milestone_status_of() {
  local id="$1"
  awk -F '\t' -v id="$id" 'NR>1 && $1==id {print $2; exit}' "$MILESTONE_STATUS" 2>/dev/null || true
}

set_milestone_status() {
  local id="$1" status="$2" tmp
  tmp="$(mktemp "$TRUST_DIR/.status.XXXXXXXX")"
  awk -F '\t' -v id="$id" 'BEGIN{OFS="\t"} NR==1 || $1!=id {print}' "$MILESTONE_STATUS" > "$tmp"
  printf '%s\t%s\n' "$id" "$status" >> "$tmp"
  mv "$tmp" "$MILESTONE_STATUS"
}

dep_satisfied() {
  local dep="$1" one
  [ -z "$dep" ] && return 0
  [ "$dep" = "-" ] && return 0
  IFS=',' read -r -a deps <<< "$dep"
  for one in "${deps[@]}"; do
    one="${one## }"; one="${one%% }"
    [ -z "$one" ] && continue
    [ "$(milestone_status_of "$one")" = ACCEPTED ] || return 1
  done
  return 0
}

select_next_milestone() {
  assert_approved
  require_clean
  [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$LAST_KNOWN_GOOD_SHA" ] || fail 'HEAD advanced outside an accepted milestone'
  # Bash collapses empty TAB-separated whitespace fields. Normalize through awk
  # to a non-whitespace separator so an empty depends_on field cannot shift the
  # review_required column and accidentally make a valid root milestone ineligible.
  while IFS='|' read -r id axis kind from to depends review; do
    [ -n "$id" ] || continue
    [ "$id" != id ] || continue
    [ "$(milestone_status_of "$id")" != ACCEPTED ] || continue
    [ "$(milestone_status_of "$id")" != BLOCKED ] || continue
    [ "$(milestone_status_of "$id")" != ACTIVE ] || fail "inconsistent active milestone: $id"
    dep_satisfied "${depends:-}" || continue
    MILESTONE_ID="$id"
    MILESTONE_AXIS="$axis"
    MILESTONE_KIND="$kind"
    MILESTONE_FROM="$from"
    MILESTONE_TO="$to"
    MILESTONE_STATUS_VALUE="READY"
    PHASE="ACTIVE"
    BASE_SHA="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" # set ONCE, never update during milestone
    HEAD_SHA="$BASE_SHA"
    verify_base_anchor
    FAST_GATE="NOT_RUN"
    MILESTONE_GATE="NOT_RUN"
    FULL_CI="$(gate_required full_ci && echo NOT_RUN || echo NOT_REQUIRED)"
    SMOKE_GATE="$(gate_required smoke && echo NOT_RUN || echo NOT_REQUIRED)"
    REVIEW_STATUS="NOT_RUN"
    REVIEW_SHA=''
    set_milestone_status "$id" ACTIVE
    AUTO_ATTEMPTS=0
    CURRENT_BLOCKER=''
    NEXT_ACTION="implement milestone $id: $axis $from -> $to while preserving all locked axes"
    write_state
    return 0
  done < <(awk -F '\t' 'BEGIN{OFS="|"} NR>1 && NF==7 {print $1,$2,$3,$4,$5,$6,$7}' "$MILESTONES")
  return 1
}

cmd_begin() {
  load_state
  [ "$STOP_REQUESTED" = 0 ] || fail 'stop requested'
  assert_approved
  if [ -n "$MILESTONE_ID" ] && [ "$MILESTONE_STATUS_VALUE" != ACCEPTED ] && [ "$MILESTONE_STATUS_VALUE" != BLOCKED ]; then
    info "Already active: $MILESTONE_ID"; return 0
  fi
  select_next_milestone || fail 'no eligible milestone'
  info "Active milestone: $MILESTONE_ID; immutable BASE_SHA=$BASE_SHA"
}

refresh_head() {
  require_clean
  [ -n "$MILESTONE_ID" ] && [ -n "$BASE_SHA" ] || fail 'no active milestone/base SHA'
  local actual
  actual="$(git rev-parse HEAD)"
  git merge-base --is-ancestor "$BASE_SHA" "$actual" || fail 'BASE_SHA is not an ancestor of HEAD'
    if [ "$actual" != "$HEAD_SHA" ]; then
    HEAD_SHA="$actual"
    FAST_GATE=NOT_RUN; MILESTONE_GATE=NOT_RUN
    FULL_CI="$(gate_required full_ci && echo NOT_RUN || echo NOT_REQUIRED)"
    SMOKE_GATE="$(gate_required smoke && echo NOT_RUN || echo NOT_REQUIRED)"
    REVIEW_STATUS=NOT_RUN; REVIEW_SHA=''
    if [ -n "$MILESTONE_ID" ]; then
      rm -f "$WORK_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID".*.tsv "$ARCHIVE_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID".*.tsv
    fi
    write_state
  fi
}

check_locked_axes() {
  assert_approved
  refresh_head
  [ "$HEAD_SHA" != "$BASE_SHA" ] || fail 'no milestone commit since immutable BASE_SHA'
  local id kind current target policy paths path rc shared before_slice after_slice
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r id kind current target policy paths; do
    [ "$id" != id ] || continue
    [ "$id" != "$MILESTONE_AXIS" ] || continue
    while IFS= read -r path; do
      [ -n "$path" ] || continue
      rc=0
      git diff --quiet "$BASE_SHA" "$HEAD_SHA" -- "$path" || rc=$?
      case "$rc" in
        0) continue ;;
        1) ;;
        *) fail "git diff failed for locked axis $id at $path" ;;
      esac
      shared=0
      path_used_by_axis "$path" "$MILESTONE_AXIS" && shared=1
      if [ "$shared" = 1 ]; then
        # Companion lockfiles are shared by design. Regenerating them for the
        # active axis is not a locked-axis move; the pin is proven on manifests/CI.
        if is_lockfile_path "$path"; then
          continue
        fi
        before_slice="$(axis_slice "$BASE_SHA" "$path" "$id" "$current")"
        after_slice="$(axis_slice "$HEAD_SHA" "$path" "$id" "$current")"
        [ -n "$before_slice" ] && [ -n "$after_slice" ] \
          || fail "BLOCKER: locked axis $id is NOT VERIFIED in shared file $path ($BASE_SHA..$HEAD_SHA)"
        [ "$before_slice" = "$after_slice" ] \
          || fail "BLOCKER: locked axis $id dependency changed in shared file $path ($BASE_SHA..$HEAD_SHA)"
      else
        fail "BLOCKER: locked axis $id changed at $path ($BASE_SHA..$HEAD_SHA)"
      fi
    done < <(normalize_source_path_list "$paths")
  done < "$AXES"
  check_milestone_scope
}

finalize_writer_commit() {
  local dirty id kind current target policy paths path file overlap ok
  local -a allowed=() entries=() to_add=()
  dirty="$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=normal)"
  [ -n "$dirty" ] || return 0
  [ -n "$MILESTONE_AXIS" ] || fail 'working tree is dirty; commit or preserve unrelated changes before validation'
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r id kind current target policy paths; do
    [ "$id" != id ] || continue
    [ "$id" = "$MILESTONE_AXIS" ] || continue
    IFS='|' read -r -a allowed <<< "$paths"
  done < "$AXES"
  [ "${#allowed[@]}" -gt 0 ] || fail 'active axis has no source_of_truth paths'
  while IFS=$'\t' read -r id kind current target policy paths; do
    [ "$id" != id ] || continue
    [ "$id" != "$MILESTONE_AXIS" ] || continue
    IFS='|' read -r -a entries <<< "$paths"
    for path in "${entries[@]}"; do
      overlap=0
      for file in "${allowed[@]}"; do
        if [ "$path" = "$file" ]; then overlap=1; break; fi
      done
      [ "$overlap" = 1 ] && continue
      git diff --quiet "$BASE_SHA" -- "$path" || fail "BLOCKER: locked axis $id changed at $path"
    done
  done < "$AXES"
  while IFS= read -r file; do
    [ -n "$file" ] || continue
    ok=0
    for path in "${allowed[@]}"; do
      if scope_match "$file" "$path"; then ok=1; break; fi
    done
    [ "$ok" = 1 ] || fail "unrelated dirty path $file; commit or preserve it before upgrade"
    to_add+=("$file")
  done < <({ git diff --name-only; git diff --cached --name-only; git ls-files --others --exclude-standard; } | sort -u)
  [ "${#to_add[@]}" -gt 0 ] && git add -- "${to_add[@]}"
  [ -n "$(git diff --cached --name-only)" ] || fail 'writer left a dirty tree with nothing to commit'
  git commit -qm "upgrade(${MILESTONE_ID}): ${MILESTONE_AXIS} ${MILESTONE_FROM} -> ${MILESTONE_TO}"
}

writer_reported_edge_block() {
  local f="${1:-$TRUST_DIR/logs/last-writer.out}"
  [ -n "${MILESTONE_ID:-}" ] || return 1
  [ -s "$f" ] || return 1
  awk -v id="$MILESTONE_ID" '
    BEGIN { if (id == "") exit 1 }
    index($0, id) == 0 { next }
    $0 == "MILESTONE EDGE: BLOCKED" { hit = 1 }
    index($0, "**BLOCKED**") { hit = 1 }
    index($0, "BLOCKED") == 1 { hit = 1 }
    END { exit !hit }
  ' "$f"
}

record_writer_edge_block() {
  local f="${1:-$TRUST_DIR/logs/last-writer.out}" evidence tmp blocked_id
  writer_reported_edge_block "$f" || return 1
  require_clean
  refresh_head
  [ "$HEAD_SHA" = "$BASE_SHA" ] || fail 'edge block requires no milestone commit (HEAD must equal BASE_SHA)'
  evidence="$(awk 'NF{gsub(/[[:space:]]+/, " "); print; exit}' "$f" | cut -c 1-240)"
  [ -n "$evidence" ] || evidence="writer blocked $MILESTONE_AXIS $MILESTONE_FROM -> $MILESTONE_TO"
  [ -f "$CONSTRAINTS" ] || printf '%s\n' $'left\trelation\tright\tevidence' > "$CONSTRAINTS"
  tmp="$(mktemp "$TRUST_DIR/.constraint.XXXXXXXX")"
  awk -F '\t' -v a="$MILESTONE_AXIS" -v t="$MILESTONE_TO" 'BEGIN{OFS="\t"} NR==1 || !($1==a && $2=="blocked_at" && $3==t) {print}' "$CONSTRAINTS" > "$tmp"
  printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$MILESTONE_AXIS" blocked_at "$MILESTONE_TO" "$evidence" >> "$tmp"
  mv -f "$tmp" "$CONSTRAINTS"
  mkdir -p "$ARCHIVE_DIR/logs"
  cp "$f" "$ARCHIVE_DIR/logs/$MILESTONE_ID.edge-blocked.md"
  blocked_id="$MILESTONE_ID"
  set_milestone_status "$blocked_id" BLOCKED
  info "Edge blocked: $blocked_id $MILESTONE_AXIS $MILESTONE_FROM -> $MILESTONE_TO (no commit; constraint recorded)"
  MILESTONE_ID=''
  MILESTONE_AXIS=''
  MILESTONE_KIND=''
  MILESTONE_FROM=''
  MILESTONE_TO=''
  MILESTONE_STATUS_VALUE=''
  BASE_SHA=''
  FAST_GATE=NOT_RUN
  MILESTONE_GATE=NOT_RUN
  REVIEW_STATUS=NOT_RUN
  REVIEW_SHA=''
  AUTO_ATTEMPTS=0
  CURRENT_BLOCKER=''
  PHASE=PLANNED
  NEXT_ACTION="edge $blocked_id blocked by compatibility; continue with next eligible milestone"
  persist_canonical_yaml
  APPROVED_PLAN_HASH="$(plan_hash)"
  write_state
  write_human_docs
}

gate_row() {
  awk -F '\t' -v m="$MILESTONE_ID" -v g="$1" 'NR>1 && $1==m && $2==g {print; exit}' "$GATES"
}
gate_required() {
  local row
  row="$(gate_row "$1")"
  [ -n "$row" ] || fail "missing gate definition for $MILESTONE_ID/$1"
  [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$row" | awk -F '\t' '{print $3}')" = true ]
}

gate_variable() {
  case "$1" in
    fast_gate) printf FAST_GATE ;; milestone_gate) printf MILESTONE_GATE ;;
    full_ci) printf FULL_CI ;; smoke) printf SMOKE_GATE ;;
    *) fail "unknown gate: $1" ;;
  esac
}

verify_gates() {
  local gate row required cwd command condition var status file sha approval spec exitcode proof_status loghash
  for gate in fast_gate milestone_gate full_ci smoke; do
    row="$(gate_row "$gate")"
    [ -n "$row" ] || fail "missing gate: $gate"
    IFS=$'\t' read -r _ _ required cwd command condition <<< "$row"
    var="$(gate_variable "$gate")"
    if [ "$required" = false ]; then
      continue
    fi
    file="$(lookup_gate_evidence_file "$MILESTONE_ID" "$gate")"
    [ -n "$file" ] && [ -f "$file" ] || fail "missing gate evidence: $gate"
    IFS=$'\t' read -r sha approval spec exitcode proof_status loghash < "$file"
    [ "$sha" = "$HEAD_SHA" ] && [ "$approval" = "$APPROVED_PLAN_HASH" ] && \
      [ "$spec" = "$(printf '%s' "$row" | hash_stream)" ] && [ "$exitcode" = 0 ] && \
      [ "$proof_status" = PASS ] || fail "stale/invalid evidence for gate: $gate"
    file="$ARCHIVE_DIR/logs/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.$HEAD_SHA.log"
    [ -f "$file" ] || file="$WORK_DIR/logs/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.$HEAD_SHA.log"
    [ -f "$file" ] && [ "$(hash_file "$file")" = "$loghash" ] || fail "missing/changed gate log: $gate"
  done
}

cmd_gate() {
  local gate="$1" row required cwd command condition var rc=0 head temp stdout stderr log success=1
  local -a gate_argv=()
  load_state
  [ "$STOP_REQUESTED" = 0 ] || fail 'stop requested'
  [ "$MILESTONE_STATUS_VALUE" != ACCEPTED ] || fail 'milestone already accepted'
  check_locked_axes
  row="$(gate_row "$gate")"
  [ -n "$row" ] || fail "unknown/missing gate: $gate"
  IFS=$'\t' read -r _ _ required cwd command condition <<< "$row"
  [ "$required" = true ] || { info "$gate: NOT_REQUIRED (approved plan)"; return 0; }
  var="$(gate_variable "$gate")"
  head="$HEAD_SHA"
  CURRENT_BUILD=RUNNING; CURRENT_BUILD_SHA="$head"
  printf -v "$var" RUNNING
  write_state
  temp="$(mktemp -d "$TRUST_DIR/.gate.XXXXXXXX")"
  stdout="$temp/stdout"; stderr="$temp/stderr"
  if [ "$AUTO_MODE" = 1 ]; then
    # No shell parsing/expansion. `&&` chains are split and each argv is exec'd.
    auto_gate_command_safe "$command" || fail "autonomous gate command is not permitted: $gate"
    local rest="$command" part
    rest="$command"
    while [ -n "$rest" ]; do
      if [[ "$rest" == *' && '* ]]; then
        part="${rest%% && *}"
        rest="${rest#* && }"
      else
        part="$rest"
        rest=""
      fi
      read -r -a gate_argv <<< "$part"
      ( cd "$ROOT/$cwd" && AI_UPGRADER_EXPECTED_SHA="$head" AI_UPGRADER_BASE_SHA="$BASE_SHA" \
          AI_UPGRADER_MILESTONE="$MILESTONE_ID" "${gate_argv[@]}" ) >> "$stdout" 2>> "$stderr" || rc=$?
      [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || break
    done
  else
    # Explicitly operator-approved manual-mode commands can use shell syntax.
    ( cd "$ROOT/$cwd" && AI_UPGRADER_EXPECTED_SHA="$head" AI_UPGRADER_BASE_SHA="$BASE_SHA" \
        AI_UPGRADER_MILESTONE="$MILESTONE_ID" bash -c "$command" ) > "$stdout" 2> "$stderr" || rc=$?
  fi
  [ "$rc" -eq 0 ] || success=0
  if [ "$condition" = sha-success ]; then
    awk -v sha="$head" '
      /^CI_SHA=/ {n++; if($0 != "CI_SHA="sha)bad=1}
      /^CI_STATUS=/ {m++; if($0 != "CI_STATUS=success")bad=1}
      END {exit !(n==1 && m==1 && !bad)}
    ' "$stdout" || success=0
  fi
  [ -z "$(git status --porcelain --untracked-files=normal)" ] || success=0
  [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$head" ] || success=0
  # If a gate changed HEAD, refresh_head invalidates every prior proof.
  refresh_head || success=0
  [ "$HEAD_SHA" = "$head" ] || success=0
  check_locked_axes || success=0
  mkdir -p "$ARCHIVE_DIR/logs" "$ARCHIVE_DIR/evidence" "$WORK_DIR/logs" "$WORK_DIR/evidence"
  log="$ARCHIVE_DIR/logs/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.$head.log"
  { printf 'command: %s\nexit: %s\nstdout:\n' "$command" "$rc"; cat "$stdout"; printf '\nstderr:\n'; cat "$stderr"; } | atomic_write "$log"
  cp "$log" "$WORK_DIR/logs/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.$head.log"
  rm -rf -- "$temp"
  if [ "$success" -eq 1 ]; then
    printf -v "$var" PASS; CURRENT_BUILD=PASS
    PHASE=GATED
  else
    printf -v "$var" FAIL; CURRENT_BUILD=FAIL
    PHASE=ACTIVE
  fi
  REVIEW_STATUS=NOT_RUN; REVIEW_SHA=''
  chmod u+w "$ARCHIVE_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.tsv" \
    "$WORK_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.tsv" 2>/dev/null || true
  printf '%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\t%s\n' "$head" "$APPROVED_PLAN_HASH" \
    "$(printf '%s' "$row" | hash_stream)" "$rc" "${!var}" "$(hash_file "$log")" \
    | atomic_write "$ARCHIVE_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.tsv"
  cp "$ARCHIVE_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.tsv" "$WORK_DIR/evidence/$MILESTONE_ID.$gate.tsv"
  chmod a-w "$log" 2>/dev/null || true
  write_state
  info "$gate: ${!var} for $head (exit=$rc)"
  [ "$success" -eq 1 ] || fail "$gate failed; milestone cannot be accepted"
}

